<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australian retail sales rise 2.7 pct in Jan.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australian retail sales rise 2.7 pct in Jan.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian retail sales rise 2.7 percent to A$10.41 billion in January, seasonally adjusted, after falling 1.0 percent to A$10.13 billion in December, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>In January 1996, retail sales rose 0.9 percent to A$10.14 billion.</p>
<p>Analysts had expected retail sales to rise a median 1.5 percent in January.  </p>
<p>Australian retail sales, January (A$ billion)</p>
<p>			  Jan 97  Dec 96 mo/mo pct Jan 96  yr/yr pct</p>
<p>    Seasonally adj   10.41   10.13   +2.7    10.14     +2.6</p>
<p>    Unadjusted	 10.26   13.20  -22.3     9.89     +3.7</p>
<p>    Trend Estimate   10.24   10.22   +0.2    10.10     +1.4</p>
<p>Retail turnover by group percentage change, seasonally adj.</p>
<p>				Jan 97	 Dec 96	 Jan 96</p>
<p>Food retailing	     +3.0	   -2.0	   +0.1</p>
<p>Department stores	  -1.0	   +0.1	   +0.5</p>
<p>Clothing, soft goods     +0.8	   +0.3	   +1.1</p>
<p>Household goods	    +4.2	   -1.8	   +1.4</p>
<p>Recreational goods	 -5.1	   +7.4	   +1.5</p>
<p>Other retailing	    +4.6	   -1.6	   +3.8</p>
<p>Hospitality, services    +6.0	   -1.9	   +1.0</p>
<p>Total			  +2.7	   -1.0	   +0.9</p>
</text>
